cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use nir-c-runtime in your research or deployment, please cite it
  using the metadata below. To cite the spikeforge toolkit that trains and
  exports the models this runtime executes, see spikeforge's own
  CITATION.cff instead.
title: nir-c-runtime
abstract: >-
  A minimal, dependency-light C11 runtime for executing NIR (Neuromorphic
  Intermediate Representation) graphs exported by spikeforge on embedded
  and edge targets where a Python/PyTorch runtime isn't an option. Loads a
  NIR JSON graph export and its weights and runs inference for spikeforge's
  conv_net topology node kinds.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Capsize Games"
    email: contact@capsizegames.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/capsize-games/nir-c-runtime"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - spiking neural networks
  - neuromorphic computing
  - NIR
  - embedded systems
  - edge inference
  - C11
